# Keep source reviewable.
#
# git classifies a blob as binary when it finds a NUL byte in the first 8000 bytes, and a binary
# blob has no diff, no line-level review comment and no three-way merge: it merges wholesale or
# conflicts wholesale. A stray control character in a template literal is enough to do it, which
# is how `apps/api/src/middleware/idempotency.ts` shipped in increment 4 with no reviewable diff.
#
# `diff` forces git to treat these paths as text anyway, so the damage is contained. It is the
# second line of defence, not the first: the `planeahead/no-literal-control-characters` ESLint
# rule (tools/eslint) fails the build on the character itself, which is the part that is loud.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ts   text diff
*.tsx  text diff
*.js   text diff
*.mjs  text diff
*.cjs  text diff
*.json text diff
*.jsonc text diff
*.md   text diff
*.yml  text diff
*.yaml text diff
*.sql  text diff

pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true
